<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Defaults compiled into the build.

Settings sync from Garmin Connect Mobile is unreliable for sideloaded (non-store)
apps. If editing these on the phone does not stick, fill them in here instead and
rebuild - that path always works.

Left empty on purpose. Filling them in bakes a real shared secret into the build,
so from that point on treat this file as a secret: mark it skip-worktree to keep
your filled-in copy out of every future commit. The README has the exact command
under "6. Watch - settings" (an XML comment cannot hold it verbatim, because the
flag's leading double hyphen is illegal in here).

Note the SDK also copies the value into garmin/garmin-settings.json, which
.gitignore already excludes.

Empty values are handled gracefully: the watch shows a red "Set server in app
settings" until both are present, so this never fails silently.
-->
<properties>
    <property id="serverUrl" type="string"></property>
    <property id="authToken" type="string"></property>
</properties>
